-- title:
--   Affine-chart residues generate the supersingular residue field, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; let $W$ be a finset of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, let $s\in W$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$; let further $K_b$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to $\bot$, and $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ cutting out $A$, henselian and discrete with maximal ideal generated by a nonzero $\varpi_b$. Giving $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and $W_0$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is everything, $W_0$ cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. Let $B$ be a subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure compatible with the inclusions into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, contained in $W_0$ (each element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$), and such that $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$: an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f h = g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$. Finally let $F_{ss}$ be a field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue field $F_{ss}$, i.e. a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ cutting out $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-multiple in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue; assume $R.\mathrm{integers}$ cuts out $W_0$ on $F_0$ and that $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$. The conclusion is twofold: every $x\in F_{ss}$ is a quotient of residues of elements of $B$, namely $x\cdot R.\mathrm{residue}(h)=R.\mathrm{residue}(g)$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $R.\mathrm{residue}(h)\neq 0$; and for $b\in B$ one has $R.\mathrm{residue}(b)=0$ if and only if the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ divides $b$.
--
--   This identifies the residue field of the regular prolongation $R$ as the fraction field of $B/\varpi_b B$, the affine chart $B$ thus reducing onto the supersingular fibre with kernel generated by the uniformiser; it is the $q=2$ case of the corresponding statement for larger $q$. It is used downstream in the construction of the semistable charts and of the Igusa-type coverings attached to the full-level modular curve at $q=2$, and in the identification of the local rings at smooth points of the reduction.
